\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{076ce0b}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The interval between two hand-offs of a pipelined load is multiplied by the size of the input in GiB, at most by 4; nothing changes below 2 GiB. On Mathlib with the machine in the native image, quiet windows, two interleaved rounds: pipelined with 8 workers 34.25 and 35.00 s before against 31.71 and 31.90 s (-8 \%), with 4 workers 55.71 against 53.80 s, with 52 publications where there were 205, 20.9 GB of garbage where there were 36.9, and 2.23 s of pauses where there were 3.75. Std and cedar are unchanged. The curve for Mathlib is then 208.3, 104.9, 53.8 and 31.8 s with 1, 2, 4 and 8 workers, and a check-only pass with 8 workers takes 27.9 s against a hardware ceiling of 26.6 s, measured with eight one-worker processes over eight shards of the file. Published with 107 tests, 104 green and 3 opt-in.}

\p{Detail: [rep-P7](rep-P7), \src{rlvm-driver/README.md}. Commit \commit{076ce0b}. Session: [profiles and prototypes](ses-JRSD). Related: [what a publication costs every worker](ins-E1DU), [the driver](design-driver).}
